WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Speaker 1: We don't usually do entertainment&nbsp;
stories on this show, but I do want to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.560
about something that happened last night.&nbsp;
Comedian Dave Chappelle was attacked on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.720
stage by an individual believed to be armed&nbsp;
while performing at the L.A. Hollywood Bowl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.640
There are a number of different videos from&nbsp;
audience members cell phones which started to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.240
flood social media, and they showed a man, a man&nbsp;
appear to run on to stage the stage and tackle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.840
Dave Chappelle. LAPD told CBS L.A. that it&nbsp;
was a 23 year old man armed with a replica&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:40.080
handgun that contained a knife blade arrested&nbsp;
and accused of assault with a deadly weapon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:47.360
Police identified him as Isaiah Lee and were&nbsp;
holding him on $30,000 bail. Dave Chappelle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.720
reportedly not injured in the attack.&nbsp;
We're not going to show a picture of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:57.040
the attacker being brought out. His arm is&nbsp;
completely mangled as a result of how he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:06.320
handled by security. And that type of imagery is&nbsp;
not allowed on many of our platforms. There is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.240
joke that was made by Chris Rock. Now, this is&nbsp;
just sort of a strange, random thing. Chris Rock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.480
who was slapped by Will Smith at the Oscars&nbsp;
recently, was in attendance, and he came up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:31.790
told the following joke after the incident.
Unidentified: Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow. Who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.360
that? Smith.
Speaker 1:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.680
Okay. So people having a good time with&nbsp;
that. So why am I talking about this?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.960
Listen. We cannot have a culture where&nbsp;
this is okay. All right. Now, initially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.840
it was sort of like asserted without evidence&nbsp;
that the attacker was a trans man attacking Dave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.320
Chappelle. For Chappelle's recently controversial&nbsp;
comments on transgenderism in a Netflix special,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.840
that that has not been demonstrated right&nbsp;
now. And if it was asserted without evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.320
and it puts the spotlight on trans people who may&nbsp;
have nothing to do with this, and even if this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.680
a trans person to group trans people under what&nbsp;
one person that that's that's absolutely terrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:26.000
if that happened. Okay. But we can't have a&nbsp;
culture where it is even remotely acceptable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.560
to do this. Now, I'm not saying we do. People&nbsp;
were mostly booing this individual. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.960
supportive of Dave Chappelle. People mostly have&nbsp;
not been supportive of Will Smith slapping Chris&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:46.640
Rock. But this is the type of thing where violence&nbsp;
begets violence and then it creates the need for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.920
you know, even more security at sporting events.&nbsp;
The same thing has been going on. There was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.320
recent NBA game. I apologize. I don't have the&nbsp;
details. It might have been the Milwaukee Bucks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.840
I'm not sure where people were running on to the&nbsp;
court. And I think there might have been some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.720
animal rights connection related to the owner&nbsp;
of the team or I don't have the details,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.960
but it's this sort of thing where people were&nbsp;
showing up and to demonstrate against the owner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.760
they were running onto the court and trying to&nbsp;
approach players. And then so you see even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:21.680
security and then you see even rougher treatment&nbsp;
of people who attempt to enter the field of play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.080
We are seeing people being assaulted for saying&nbsp;
things that others don't like. Now I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:39.280
make a clear line here. I am sensitive to the idea&nbsp;
that sometimes there are forms of speech that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:45.440
violent towards groups of people. Okay. So&nbsp;
you can make the case that banning abortion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:50.400
which is a legislative act that a state can do.&nbsp;
This has been it's a big topic, so I'm choosing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.840
this one. You could say banning abortion is a form&nbsp;
of violence against women. I'm sensitive to that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:03.280
I am absolutely sensitive to that. But we're not&nbsp;
going to solve it by showing up and attacking the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.400
legislators. We're going to solve it by voting&nbsp;
all of them out, putting in legislators that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.880
legalize abortion. That's the path forward.&nbsp;
And we could always say, Yeah, but but it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.520
gerrymandering and it's stacked against us. Well,&nbsp;
then we got to fix that. I have not seen evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.280
that just physically attacking the individuals&nbsp;
who say the things we don't like is an acceptable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:30.000
means of change. And I recognize the difference&nbsp;
between. The action of banning abortion. Versus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.920
Dave Chappelle saying something in a special&nbsp;
people don't like. Those are two different things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.040
I don't believe violence is going&nbsp;
to be the solution in either. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.520
we all have to condemn this stuff. We can condemn&nbsp;
the things Dave Chappelle said, but we also have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:49.520
to condemn the violence. And it's I don't like the&nbsp;
direction that this is going. And I want to hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.840
from you in the audience as to your perspective&nbsp;
on what I think is an unfortunately growing trend.

